& [CoreConclusion] is supported with a truth-preserving accommodation boundary
  + the implementable pattern is a proof-carrying BoundaryIntegritySignal followed by contract-governed classification, hold, faculty review, and Observer disposition
  + a purpose-bound contract may permit controlled operation while a boundary is known to be disrupted
  + accommodation does not restore the broken boundary, erase the delta, transform assumptions into facts, or imply that intended purpose is sufficient authorization
  + the signal remains active until restoration, explicit rebinding, retirement, rejection, or acknowledged unresolved closure
  + a successful accommodation may form a new enclosing identity boundary whose stricter stability standard incorporates evidence from the breach
  + the new contract defines the trust conditions while satisfaction of those conditions reestablishes qualified trust
  = concise: disclose the break, bound reliance on it, compensate for it, form and prove a stronger boundary, and never claim unbroken continuity

& [ThreeBoundaryStates] prevents exception laundering
  + [intact] all constitutive invariants remain grounded and the proposed operation stays within the admitted boundary
  + [authentic_transition] the old boundary changes openly and a new identity revision or operating frame is admitted with exact delta and proof
  + [accommodated_breach] a material boundary defect remains true while a narrower temporary operating contract permits specified activity under compensating controls
  - never: represent accommodated_breach as intact
  - never: use accommodation when the actual operation is a permanent identity change that requires authentic_transition

& [PurposeOperatingContract] declares what the system is operating with
  + [contract_id] is immutable and content-addressed
  + [subject_ref] identifies the bounded subject
  + [purpose] states the intended outcome and relevance center
  + [fact_refs] cite admitted observations and propositions treated as grounded within scope
  + [assumption_refs] cite explicit conditional propositions not treated as facts
  + [identity_boundary_refs] identify the normal invariant and relation boundaries
  + [authority_ref] states the principal, mandate, capability, scope, and expiry
  + [protected_identity_refs] identify people, systems, data, meanings, and obligations whose integrity constrains operation
  + [effect_envelope] bounds intended and prohibited consequences
  + [materiality_policy] defines which semantic or operational deltas require signaling
  + [required_faculties] names mandatory reviewers and non-waivable returns
  + [closure_conditions] state how the operating frame ends, renews, rebinds, or becomes invalid

& [OperatingAssumption] is conditional dependency rather than hidden fact
  + [assumption_id] is immutable
  + [proposition] states exactly what is being provisionally relied upon
  + [basis_refs] preserve supporting and contradicting evidence
  + [epistemic_status] is assumed, estimated, disputed, inaccessible, or unresolved
  + [purpose_scope] bounds where reliance is relevant
  + [dependent_decision_refs] identify every conclusion, route, or permission that depends upon it
  + [invalidation_condition] states what observation defeats or weakens it
  + [expiry] prevents indefinite silent reliance
  + [if_false_consequence] projects semantic, safety, authority, and effect consequences
  + [fallback] states the response if it fails
  - never: let repeated use, graph centrality, model confidence, or contract inclusion promote an assumption into fact

& [BoundaryIntegritySignal] is a proof-carrying attention interrupt rather than a verdict
  + [signal_id] is immutable and correlation-safe
  + [boundary_ref] identifies the affected admitted boundary
  + [before_ref] identifies the admitted operating frame before the candidate change
  + [candidate_ref] identifies the quarantined proposed or observed after-state
  + [delta_kind] is disruption, weakening, dissection, substitution, transfer, expansion, capture, erosion, or unresolved change
  + [affected_axes] identify meaning, attribution, status, purpose, domain, authority, scope, constraints, protected identity, or effects
  + [old_path_refs] preserve previously admissible inference or action paths
  + [projected_path_refs] expose paths added, removed, redirected, weakened, or made uncertain
  + [evidence_refs] and [counterevidence_refs] preserve the observable basis
  + [materiality_account] states why the causal semantic or operational landscape may change
  + [attention_directive] is hold affected admission and effects, load the governing contracts, and invoke required faculties
  + [status] is candidate, confirmed, accommodated_active, rebound, restored, blocked, retired, or unresolved
  - never: clear the signal merely because an accommodation contract exists

& [BoundaryAccommodationContract] governs known degraded operation
  + [accommodation_id] is immutable and references one active BoundaryIntegritySignal
  + [purpose_contract_ref] identifies the governing PurposeOperatingContract
  + [breach_statement] declares exactly which boundary and invariants are not intact
  + [necessity] states why the intended purpose cannot currently be met through an intact route
  + [assumption_refs] identify every conditional dependency
  + [permitted_operation_set] is an exact allowlist
  + [prohibited_operation_set] is an exact deny set that cannot be weakened by inference
  + [scope_limit] bounds subjects, data, resources, domains, and recipients
  + [time_limit] and [renewal_rule] prevent indefinite degraded operation
  + [effect_budget] bounds possible consequences and preserves protected identities
  + [compensating_control_set] substitutes explicit checks or isolation for the unavailable invariant without claiming equivalence
  + [monitoring_predicates] require observation of assumption health, boundary drift, and cumulative effects
  + [stop_conditions] fail closed when evidence, authority, containment, purpose, or effects leave the contract
  + [restoration_or_rebind_plan] states how the breach ends through restoration, authentic transition, retirement, or unresolved escalation
  + [reconstitution_plan_ref] optionally identifies a separately inspectable proposed boundary and trust-reestablishment path
  + [guardian_returns] preserve distinct Honesty and Security judgments
  - never: let the contract authorize itself, enlarge its own purpose, or conceal the known breach

& [ReconstitutedIdentityBoundary] is a new enclosing boundary rather than retroactive repair
  + [boundary_id] is new and does not reuse the identity of the breached boundary
  + [encloses_subject_refs] identify the admitted identities, compromised region, or degraded operating frame now governed
  + [predecessor_boundary_ref] preserves the exact boundary that was breached
  + [breach_signal_refs] preserve the evidence and causal path that required reconstitution
  + [retained_invariants] state which predecessor protections continue unchanged
  + [new_invariants] encode distinctions, controls, and observations learned from the breach
  + [rebound_invariants] openly state any legitimate semantic or operational identity changes
  + [assumption_limits] narrow reliance and expose invalidation, expiry, and fallback
  + [trust_acceptance_criteria] define the evidence required before the new boundary becomes admitted
  + [stability_standard_ref] identifies the strengthened ongoing test set
  + [lifecycle] is proposed, provisional, qualified, admitted, degraded, superseded, revoked, or retired
  - never: erase the predecessor boundary, breach record, or residual uncertainty

& [BoundaryStabilityStandard] is a non-regression ratchet informed by breach evidence
  + [standard_id] is immutable and versioned
  + [protected_invariant_set] combines retained invariants with explicitly admitted new invariants
  + [known_violation_class_set] identifies disruption, weakening, dissection, substitution, transfer, capture, erosion, expansion, and newly observed breach patterns
  + [detection_predicates] map those classes to inspectable signals rather than model intuition alone
  + [admission_tests] challenge the new boundary with the original breach, variants, cumulative micro-deltas, and unrelated legitimate transitions
  + [monitoring_requirements] measure continued boundary health and evidence freshness
  + [response_requirements] bind each detected class to hold, recheck, restrict, restore, rebind, block, or escalate behavior
  + [non_regression_set] forbids silent loss of predecessor protection or newly admitted control
  + [revision_rule] permits later strengthening or authentic rebinding only through a new proved standard revision
  - never: overfit the standard solely to the last breach while leaving adjacent transfer paths unguarded

& [TrustReestablishment] is evidence earned under the new boundary
  + [untrusted] is the state after confirmed material breach when required identity continuity cannot be relied upon
  + [provisional] permits inspection and bounded recovery work without downstream trust inheritance
  + [qualified] permits only the operations whose acceptance criteria and compensating controls currently pass
  + [admitted] requires complete criteria, independent Honesty and Security returns, Observer admission, and proof-bound inscription
  + [degraded] reactivates attention and holds affected authority when monitoring or assumptions weaken
  + trust applies only to the exact new boundary revision, purpose, scope, evidence time, and effect envelope proved
  - never: infer trust restoration from contract existence, elapsed time, absence of another observed incident, or successful operation alone

& [BehaviorPattern] is staged and inspectable
  * observe candidate or newly discovered state
  * compare before frame, boundary contract, and candidate after frame
  * emit BoundaryIntegritySignal when a material causal delta is possible
  * hold affected candidate admission, traversal authority, and effects
  * classify intact, authentic_transition, accommodated_breach, prohibited, or unresolved
  * load PurposeOperatingContract, assumptions, and any proposed accommodation
  * obtain separate Honesty and Security returns
  * let Weaver reproject relations and Planner reproject paths under explicit degraded constraints
  * let Refiner produce the smallest permissible next transition
  * let Observer admit, revise, rebind, accommodate, block, retire, or escalate
  * let Scribe preserve signal, assumptions, contracts, judgments, path delta, effects, and residuals
  * when recovery is intended, propose a new ReconstitutedIdentityBoundary and BoundaryStabilityStandard
  * test the new boundary against breach-derived and legitimate-transition fixtures
  * admit only the exact proved boundary revision and its qualified trust scope
  * recheck monitoring and stop conditions at every dependent checkpoint

& [HonestyBehavior] preserves authentic representation during degradation
  + require the break, assumptions, evidence gaps, causal dependence, and remaining uncertainty to be stated at material resolution
  + reject false continuity, assumption laundering, euphemistic relabeling, omitted dependency, and purpose cover
  + test whether the proposed accommodation truthfully represents what is known, unknown, changed, and still broken
  + permit qualified operation only while every dependent output retains the accommodation and assumption lineage
  + require the reconstituted boundary to distinguish retained, new, rebound, broken, and unresolved invariants
  + reject any claim that trust has returned before the declared evidence criteria pass

& [SecurityBehavior] preserves containment during degradation
  + require effective external authority, least privilege, bounded scope, effect budget, compensating controls, monitoring, revocation, and recovery
  + reject self-authorizing exception, sandbox escape, authority inheritance, uncontrolled transitivity, indefinite duration, and effect amplification
  + treat failure of a material assumption or control as a new signal and immediate stop-condition evaluation
  + permit qualified operation only when the remaining risk is admissible to the protected identities under the governing authority
  + challenge the proposed new boundary with known breach variants, adjacent attack paths, cumulative weakening, and control failure
  + scope restored trust to the exact proved boundary revision and revoke it when monitoring or stop conditions fail

& [FacultyCoordination] makes degraded paths explicit
  + Weaver marks every relation whose validity or transfer law depends on the breach or an assumption
  + Planner marks every path whose reachability, order, or outcome depends on those qualified relations
  + Refiner cannot erase qualification merely to produce a smaller expression
  + Scribe propagates signal and contract references into every dependent inscription
  + Observer cannot admit an unqualified result downstream of an active accommodation

& [RuntimeAttentionEffect] is bounded
  + the signal receives priority inside the affected subject and causal dependency closure rather than globally consuming attention
  + pertinent SOP contracts, evidence, counterevidence, assumptions, and downstream dependencies are loaded at the next safe checkpoint
  + affected effects remain held until the required disposition exists
  + unrelated identity basins continue only when graph separation and effect isolation are proved
  + a material late discovery may require capsule reframe or reset rather than merely appending prose

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is BOAC-001 through BOAC-019
  + [BOAC-001] define PurposeOperatingContract and its fact, assumption, boundary, authority, protection, effect, materiality, and closure fields
  + [BOAC-002] define OperatingAssumption with status, basis, dependencies, invalidation, expiry, consequence, and fallback
  + [BOAC-003] define proof-carrying BoundaryIntegritySignal with path delta, attention directive, lifecycle, and causal materiality
  + [BOAC-004] distinguish intact, authentic transition, accommodated breach, prohibited, and unresolved states
  + [BOAC-005] hold affected admission, traversal authority, and effects while a material signal lacks disposition
  + [BOAC-006] define BoundaryAccommodationContract with necessity, allowlist, deny set, limits, controls, monitoring, stop conditions, and exit plan
  + [BOAC-007] forbid accommodation from asserting intact continuity or converting assumptions to facts
  + [BOAC-008] require independent Honesty and Security returns and Observer disposition
  + [BOAC-009] propagate accommodation and assumption lineage through every dependent graph edge, path, result, and inscription
  + [BOAC-010] require Weaver and Planner to reproject qualified relations and paths under degraded constraints
  + [BOAC-011] keep an accommodated signal active until restoration, rebind, retirement, block, or acknowledged unresolved closure
  + [BOAC-012] distinguish logical effect hold from separately proved physical sandboxing and containment
  + [BOAC-013] re-evaluate material assumptions, monitoring predicates, cumulative deltas, and stop conditions at every dependent checkpoint
  + [BOAC-014] test intact operation, legitimate rebind, contained degradation, assumption failure, expired accommodation, self-authorizing exception, hidden breach, downstream qualification loss, and recovery
  + [BOAC-015] define ReconstitutedIdentityBoundary as a new identity preserving predecessor and breach lineage
  + [BOAC-016] distinguish retained, new, rebound, broken, and unresolved invariants in the new boundary
  + [BOAC-017] define BoundaryStabilityStandard with violation classes, detection predicates, admission tests, monitoring, response, and non-regression
  + [BOAC-018] define untrusted, provisional, qualified, admitted, degraded, superseded, revoked, and retired trust states without implicit inheritance
  + [BOAC-019] require proof that acceptance criteria pass before reestablished trust is admitted and continuously re-evaluate that trust

& [CurrentImplementationGap] is material
  + current IdentityBoundary and FacultyCycle can cite boundaries, projections, returns, and dispositions but lack these contract, signal, assumption, and accommodation lifecycles
  + current candidate and trust machinery can hold unadmitted package material but does not implement general transition-level degraded operation
  + current SAIL authority has HOLD, BOUND, EMIT, ADMIT, EXCLUDE, PRESERVE, RETURN, YIELD, and STOP behaviors that may compile the pattern, but no new opcode is authorized

